WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.600
I'm definitely gonna be the first-star idol!

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.520
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!

00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.570
So far on Aikatsu Stars!

00:00:12.070 --> 00:00:18.490
Futaba Aria-chan, a super cute idol from Finland, came here to be the new muse of My Little Heart.

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:23.410
So pure and innocent you just can't leave her alone, she's like a real live fairy.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:31.420
During the debut performance for her My Little Heart Premium Rare Dress, she managed to get Star Wings.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.010
Her arrival has brightened my outlook on Aikatsu even more.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:38.140
I'll become the world's brightest star.

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.720
And so starts another day of Aikatsu!

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:50.440
We meet again, Japan.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.400
Only one pair of Star Wings remain.

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:56.320
Be still, my heart. {fuck you sources that say this is used ironically in modern times, you can't take this from me}{you're using it unironically, ironically}

00:00:58.870 --> 00:00:59.580
Ouch!

00:00:59.580 --> 00:01:02.290
Goodness, what is the matter now?

00:01:02.290 --> 00:01:03.250
What's up?

00:01:03.250 --> 00:01:04.660
What happened?

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.290
It's incredible. Aria-chan is amazing.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:14.170
How did she ascend that fast?

00:01:14.170 --> 00:01:18.930
No wonder she was able to nab Star Wings at her first appearance as muse.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:23.020
Then she strung together top-notch 
performances to bring her to this point.

00:01:23.020 --> 00:01:24.930
I knew she could do it.

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:28.980
She's holding another event.

00:01:28.980 --> 00:01:32.150
I'm looking forward to it so much I can't contain my excitement!

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:10.210
What do you think?

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.710
We're finally back in Japan!

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:17.420
Oh, I see. So you're really happy!

00:03:17.420 --> 00:03:18.920
Kirara-chan!

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:22.140
Yume-chan!

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.720
Welcome home. {wait for it}

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.060
I wasn't expecting all this. How've you been?

00:03:30.390 --> 00:03:32.060
Should I call this your home?

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.110
I'm back! {either she means in the way of "you were literally just here a week ago" or like this}{like this}

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.190
Huh? Where're the others?

00:03:36.190 --> 00:03:38.480
They got called in to work unexpectedly.

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:43.870
Aw man. And here I brought you all sweets from around the world to share.

00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.580
Right, Carol-ta...{this doesn't sound much like tan}{fine, it's actually this}

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:48.740
Huh? Where'd she go?

00:04:04.050 --> 00:04:06.800
Oh? Hello there!

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:10.680
Fluffy puffy... You're very fluffy puffy!

00:04:10.680 --> 00:04:12.060
Aria-chan.

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.060
Yume-chan!

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.690
What brings you here?

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.440
Hime-chan brought me along.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:18.770
She did?

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:19.690
Yes.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:23.860
Hime-chan said she had something to take care of and went inside the ship to play,

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.450
but then the seagulls called me outside, and I couldn't get back in.

00:04:28.450 --> 00:04:30.080
So you got lost.

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:34.750
You're the Futaba Aria-chan everyone's talking about?

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:38.040
I'm Hanazono Kirara! Nice to meet you.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.880
It's nice to meet you too.

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.800
Please accept this.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:47.090
So cute!

00:04:47.090 --> 00:04:50.680
In flower language, jasmine means "lovable".

00:04:51.520 --> 00:04:53.350
It suits you wonderfully, Kirara-san.

00:04:54.810 --> 00:04:56.100
Thank you!

00:04:56.100 --> 00:04:58.730
So you think I'm adorable, huh?

00:04:58.730 --> 00:05:00.610
You've got good eyes, Aria-chan!

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:04.240
Okay! I'll show you all around Venus Ark!

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:08.820
Good idea. There's a lot of Aikatsu that'll surprise you here.

00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:10.740
Surprising Aikatsu?

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:14.120
Yes! Don't you wanna see?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:17.330
I'm fascinated... I'm very fascinated!

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:22.510
I was a tad shocked when I heard you would step down as muse,

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.880
but as a result, you obtained the Jupiter Star Wings.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.470
Quite splendid.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:30.510
It was all Aria-chan's doing.

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:34.020
Only she could have been granted those wings.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:36.230
What do you intend to do next?

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:38.900
Perhaps found a new brand?

00:05:38.900 --> 00:05:40.650
I wonder about that.

00:05:40.650 --> 00:05:44.650
Hime, it's high time you return to the stage.

00:05:44.650 --> 00:05:46.900
I will when the time is right.

00:05:46.900 --> 00:05:50.120
For now, I want to enjoy Aria-chan's Aikatsu.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:53.910
What reason do you have to devote all your attention on her?

00:05:56.250 --> 00:06:02.550
Very well. Show me how far those wings can take Aria Futaba.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:04.800
Let's Elzacise!

00:06:04.800 --> 00:06:07.300
Let's Elzacise!

00:06:10.300 --> 00:06:13.310
Aikatsu! Aikatsu!

00:06:14.220 --> 00:06:16.810
It's a mountain. Where did it come from?

00:06:16.810 --> 00:06:19.850
Basically, we have cutting-edge facilities!

00:06:19.850 --> 00:06:23.190
We can do Aikatsu anywhere in the world with them.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:24.610
One more set!

00:06:28.530 --> 00:06:30.280
It's beautiful!

00:06:30.280 --> 00:06:33.080
Is this my homeland?{I guess}

00:06:35.240 --> 00:06:38.710
But I can't hear the sound of the wind or the trees.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:40.080
Is it fake?

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:43.170
Fake? You can't call it that, or...

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:43.960
Baa!

00:06:44.250 --> 00:06:47.920
You should just be happy and accept it!

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:55.680
What will you show me next? 
I want to see surprising Aikatsu!

00:06:57.270 --> 00:06:58.680
How about...

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.310
Huh?

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.440
Aikatsu!

00:07:04.440 --> 00:07:06.070
Aikatsu!

00:07:08.690 --> 00:07:11.740
What are you doing? Is it Aikatsu?

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:13.570
Y-Yes, it is.

00:07:13.570 --> 00:07:17.080
How cool... it's very cool! {I'd like to use something else}

00:07:17.080 --> 00:07:18.950
Aren't you...

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:20.500
Please take this.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:24.250
In flower language, yucca means "gallant".

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.250
It's perfect for a prince like you!

00:07:26.250 --> 00:07:27.960
A prince?

00:07:28.420 --> 00:07:31.380
Thank you. It's a lovely flower.

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:34.260
Huh?

00:07:36.470 --> 00:07:40.100
<i>Come to think of it, I didn't sense her presence at all.</i>

00:07:41.100 --> 00:07:44.060
<i>She appeared before me in an instant.{something something sneaked not snuck}</i>

00:07:44.610 --> 00:07:48.030
<i>Futaba Aria is a mysterious girl.</i>

00:07:49.240 --> 00:07:51.700
Where did she wander off to?

00:07:51.700 --> 00:07:56.870
This happened before. Last time, I found her taking a nap in a field of flowers.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:58.490
A field of flowers?

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.370
I know just the place!

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:04.040
What is the name of this one?

00:08:04.040 --> 00:08:08.250
Those are <i>Humilis Alba Coerulea Ocula</i>.{by the way, this is a mistake. It should be Oculata}{yeah, they're be-eyed, not eyes}

00:08:08.250 --> 00:08:10.630
H-Humilis?

00:08:11.090 --> 00:08:14.140
A type of tulip commonly known as star sapphire.

00:08:14.140 --> 00:08:17.140
It is quite the rare flower.

00:08:17.140 --> 00:08:20.520
Pretty... it's very pretty!

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.770
I knew you'd be here!

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.520
Geez, we were worried about you.

00:08:25.520 --> 00:08:29.900
I'm sorry! I was just drawn here by the sound of the flowers.

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:33.280
Oh, I also met a prince along the way!

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:35.160
A prince?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:41.660
I requested her assistance in watering the flowers. My apologies.

00:08:41.660 --> 00:08:43.370
No, it's fine.

00:08:44.420 --> 00:08:45.670
Mister!

00:08:45.670 --> 00:08:48.420
This one doesn't look healthy.

00:08:48.420 --> 00:08:51.710
The bugs have gotten to it recently.

00:08:51.710 --> 00:08:55.090
I've done my utmost, but it is beyond my ability.

00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.700
Oh my!

00:09:16.740 --> 00:09:19.240
It looks like a bird in flight!

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:21.620
I've never seen a flower like this before!

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:26.500
Neither have I! How cute! How very cute!

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:29.210
The rest of the garden seems livelier as well.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.460
I have heard of this phenomenon before.

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:37.260
It is said that playing music for plants relieves their stress and helps them grow.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:40.760
It feels like my heart has been calmed too.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:41.640
Me too!

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:49.230
Aria-sama, please allow me to treat you as a token of my appreciation.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:58.070
This is British tea of the highest grade.

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.660
It has a pleasant scent.

00:10:00.660 --> 00:10:02.700
There are plenty of snacks too.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:06.210
We bought famous treats from all over.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:08.540
Thank you.

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.210
Then I'll indulge.

00:10:12.250 --> 00:10:14.300
This tastes familiar!

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:16.920
I believe that is from a Nordic country.

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:20.300
It might be chocolate from Finland.

00:10:20.300 --> 00:10:22.470
Yes, it's delicious.

00:10:22.470 --> 00:10:25.770
Hey, hey, what kind of place is Finland?

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:31.110
There are abundant forests and majestic lakes. You can even see the aurora at night.

00:10:31.110 --> 00:10:34.190
The great nature of Finland is my everything.{this is not okay, but okay}

00:10:34.190 --> 00:10:35.230
Wow.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:39.030
Okay then, so why did you decide to come to Japan?

00:10:39.030 --> 00:10:43.080
Nothing made me happier than singing.

00:10:43.080 --> 00:10:47.200
Everyone said that listening to me sing made them smile.

00:10:48.290 --> 00:10:51.420
My happiness could make everyone smile.

00:10:52.330 --> 00:10:55.960
I was so enamored in that joy that I did Aikatsu every day.

00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:00.840
One day, Hime-chan came to see me.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:06.850
Your Aikatsu can bring smiles to many more people.

00:11:06.850 --> 00:11:07.770
Huh?

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:12.310
I'm one of them. Won't you come with me?

00:11:12.310 --> 00:11:15.230
We'll flood the world with smiles.

00:11:19.190 --> 00:11:22.110
So that's why you came with Hime-chan.

00:11:22.110 --> 00:11:27.120
Yes. I want to learn a lot more and bring smiles all around the world.

00:11:29.290 --> 00:11:30.580
I got it!

00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.460
What did you get?

00:11:32.460 --> 00:11:36.090
A place that'll surprise and delight Aria-chan!

00:11:51.480 --> 00:11:59.110
Behold! A place filled with the history of dresses, music, and dances from around the globe!

00:11:59.110 --> 00:12:01.650
It's the World Aikatsu Room!

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.660
This is amazing!

00:12:04.660 --> 00:12:07.790
There are so many dresses I've never even imagined.

00:12:07.790 --> 00:12:13.460
If you wanna make people around the world smile, you've gotta learn about the whole world first.

00:12:14.670 --> 00:12:17.170
This is a kimono, a Japanese dress. {says the New Zealander in front of a Japanese}

00:12:17.170 --> 00:12:19.710
Doesn't it have a pretty design?

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:24.220
Lovely... it's very lovely!

00:12:27.930 --> 00:12:29.930
Guess what this is!

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:36.360
Classical music. Liebesträume by Franz Liszt. {we can do dreams of love too I guess}{it's a collection of three pieces though, each an individual dream of love, so we should careful the wording}

00:12:36.940 --> 00:12:39.980
Correct! What about this?

00:12:42.820 --> 00:12:46.450
It's very cheerful and makes me want to dance!

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.540
I have never heard this before. What is it?

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:50.950
Samba!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:54.000
Just as you thought, it's dance music.

00:12:58.590 --> 00:13:01.710
They appear to be praying.

00:13:01.710 --> 00:13:07.720
That's right! Hula dance isn't just for 
entertainment—it's a prayer to the gods.

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.100
The gods? {I did check, Hawaii does have multiple}

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:13.230
I feel like I might start to cry.

00:13:14.350 --> 00:13:16.400
I ran out of space.

00:13:16.400 --> 00:13:18.730
But I still want to see more!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.860
It's getting late, but come and hang out anytime.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:27.780
There is so much here I've never seen before. Why is that?

00:13:27.780 --> 00:13:30.740
That's because Elza-sama's the owner.

00:13:30.740 --> 00:13:32.290
Elza-sama?

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:39.000
Elza-sama collects perfect things from around the world for her school, so we've got all sorts of Aikatsu here.

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:43.210
Aren't you glad you got to learn all sorts of new things today?

00:13:43.210 --> 00:13:47.550
Yes! It makes me as happy as singing.

00:13:47.550 --> 00:13:49.680
Could this also be...

00:13:49.680 --> 00:13:51.760
Of course, it's Aikatsu!

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:55.230
Venus Ark is full of surprises...

00:13:55.230 --> 00:13:57.310
It's very surprising!

00:14:00.810 --> 00:14:05.780
Seeing you so happy makes me really happy too.

00:14:05.780 --> 00:14:07.070
Kirara too!

00:14:08.610 --> 00:14:11.370
Well, Aria-chan? Did you have fun?

00:14:11.370 --> 00:14:13.370
Yes, very much.

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:18.210
So did I. You left me speechless when you sang for the flowers.

00:14:19.630 --> 00:14:23.630
I simply love flowers and nature.

00:14:23.630 --> 00:14:28.300
I can see that. You grew up surrounded by nature.

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:29.260
Yes!

00:14:29.260 --> 00:14:33.140
You know what? I just got a great idea.

00:14:33.760 --> 00:14:34.600
{do we really need to these? also wasn't there one earlier that you didn't?}{I wanted to just give it to them}

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:38.390
That does sound like a splendid idea.

00:14:38.390 --> 00:14:40.270
Let's make it happen.

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:43.110
I'm glad you like it. I'll work hard to make it real.

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:44.360
Thank you.

00:14:45.820 --> 00:14:49.950
You were a great help in looking after Aria-chan today.

00:14:50.410 --> 00:14:55.700
It was my pleasure. Whenever we're together, I can't help but keep my eyes on her.

00:14:56.750 --> 00:14:57.910
Me neither.

00:14:57.910 --> 00:15:00.790
I want to know more about her allure.

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:04.550
And I'm sure her fans feel the same way too.

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:07.050
You've become so reliable, Yume-chan.

00:15:08.010 --> 00:15:12.430
It's all thanks to you and all you've done for me.

00:15:12.430 --> 00:15:15.430
Now it's my turn to do the same for Aria-chan.

00:15:15.430 --> 00:15:17.680
Yes, please do.

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:29.950
Huh? Wasn't this supposed to be held in the Hall? {grand hall iirc}

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.070
It was changed at the last minute.

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.460
Here, wear this.

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:42.210
Thanks!

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:45.130
That's so cute! I'm getting into this!

00:15:45.130 --> 00:15:46.340
Yeah!

00:15:49.260 --> 00:15:50.800
This gets me going!{me too}

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.300
I'm in!

00:15:53.680 --> 00:15:54.800
It feels good!

00:15:55.300 --> 00:15:58.560
I haven't walked barefoot in so long.

00:16:00.890 --> 00:16:02.270
Nature...

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:03.690
Sure is nice.

00:16:17.830 --> 00:16:20.200
Please listen closely.

00:16:20.200 --> 00:16:24.580
The sound of wind. The sound of flowers. The sound of greenery.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:31.630
All of those sounds make up the rhythms of nature.

00:16:32.220 --> 00:16:36.220
When the rhythms combine, a melody is born!

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:53.320
Futaba Aria—May the flower of Aikatsu bloom!

00:17:15.630 --> 00:17:18.010
Dresses are a charm for beauty! {tried a thing? like with good luck charm}{I think if you want to try a thing you this, but you can also just "Dresses are a charm for beauty" or "Dresses are a good luck charm," if you don't will}

00:20:13.350 --> 00:20:15.230
That was unbelievable!

00:20:15.230 --> 00:20:17.980
It was like I could see the nature of Finland.

00:20:17.980 --> 00:20:20.440
She's no ordinary girl!

00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:22.860
We'll have to push ourselves even more.

00:20:22.860 --> 00:20:24.990
Look at the waves of smiles!

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:27.490
She was truly wonderful.

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:28.990
Aria-chan!

00:20:34.880 --> 00:20:36.500
Yay!

00:20:37.090 --> 00:20:39.550
You accomplished your goal, Aria-chan.

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.510
I couldn't have done it without you.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:44.890
It felt as if I were singing in Finland.

00:20:44.890 --> 00:20:47.760
This event captured you perfectly.

00:20:48.930 --> 00:20:51.310
I'm sure I only could've done it here.

00:20:51.310 --> 00:20:55.520
I know! Why don't I show you around Four Star next time?

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.690
Really? Please do.

00:21:03.700 --> 00:21:05.910
That was a fabulous performance.

00:21:05.910 --> 00:21:09.370
Thank you very much, um...

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:12.160
I am Elza Forte.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:13.660
It's you!

00:21:14.790 --> 00:21:17.670
Is that everything you've got?

00:21:19.130 --> 00:21:22.300
Everything about me comes from Finland.

00:21:22.800 --> 00:21:26.470
I used to think that was good enough, but...

00:21:26.470 --> 00:21:30.680
Then I learned the world was full of unfamiliar things.

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:37.190
The world is vast. There are innumerable types of Aikatsu you have yet to experience.{did you lose your pieces?}

00:21:37.520 --> 00:21:40.320
New... Aikatsu.

00:21:40.730 --> 00:21:44.610
Aira Futaba! Come to Venus Ark!

00:21:49.450 --> 00:21:51.580
Here, Elza-san.

00:21:53.200 --> 00:21:56.540
In flower language, the carnation means "insatiable curiosity". {according to jisho, 'spirit of inquiry'}

00:21:57.460 --> 00:22:01.750
I want to know more... about new Aikatsu.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:04.050
I very much want to know!

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.890
Do you accept this?

00:22:10.890 --> 00:22:15.140
Of course. Aria-chan's Aikatsu belongs to her alone.

00:22:15.640 --> 00:22:17.310
We're all set then.

00:22:19.650 --> 00:22:21.820
I'll be in your care.

00:23:55.780 --> 00:24:01.330
I'll do my best Aikatsu as Hime-chan's 
successor at My Little Heart in this dress!

00:24:01.330 --> 00:24:04.750
Be sure to do lots of Aikatsu with us from now on!

00:24:04.750 --> 00:24:09.260
I want to know more. I very much want to know more about new Aikatsu!

